From: IdentityV on Mac maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] winecoreaudio: normalize capture ring read offset after overflow

The circular distance added to lcl_offs_frames can cross the end of the
local capture ring. Keeping the unnormalised sum makes GetCaptureBuffer
subtract a larger offset from bufsize_frames and return an out-of-bounds
pointer. Preserve the existing overflow policy but keep the ring invariant.

This fixes a reproducible buffer-boundary defect in CodeWeavers 26.1; it is
not evidence that this overflow caused the reported voice-playback artifact.
Apply after the current default-device-following patch series.

--- a/dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c
+++ b/dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c
@@ -1361,6 +1361,8 @@
         if(stream->held_frames + produced_frames > stream->bufsize_frames){
             stream->lcl_offs_frames += buf_ptr_diff(stream->lcl_offs_frames, stream->wri_offs_frames,
                                                     stream->bufsize_frames);
+            /* The oldest retained frame must stay inside the circular buffer. */
+            stream->lcl_offs_frames %= stream->bufsize_frames;
             stream->held_frames = stream->bufsize_frames;
         }else
             stream->held_frames += produced_frames;
